    "body": "Fixes #29422\n\n## Motivation\n\nA pruned node can end up with an empty chainstate (the UTXO database) while its\nblock index already records that the genesis block was pruned. In that state the\nnode cannot start: an empty chainstate is rebuilt by connecting blocks from\ngenesis, but the genesis block data is gone, so no tip can ever be connected. On\ncurrent master the node waits for a chain tip indefinitely and never prints an\nactionable error. (The assertion failure in getBlockHash() reported in #29422\nwas against an older version; on master it hangs instead.)\n\nHow the node reaches this state: during a flush, FlushStateToDisk() writes the\nblock index before it writes the coins database. If the process is interrupted\nbetween those two writes during the chainstate's first flush, and that flush also\nprunes block files, the on-disk block index marks the early blocks (including\ngenesis) as no longer stored, while the coins database was never written. An OOM\nkill during IBD on a low-memory machine is one way to hit this; deleting the\nchainstate directory of a pruned node produces the same on-disk state.\n\n## Change\n\nDuring chainstate initialization, when a chainstate's coins view is empty, check\nwhether the genesis block is known to the block index but has had its block data\npruned. If so, return ChainstateLoadStatus::FAILURE instead of continuing into\nthe wait-for-tip path. The existing failure handling then tells the user to\nrestart with -reindex, and the GUI offers its usual reindex prompt.\n\nNormal startup, a first startup on an empty datadir, and an explicit -reindex are\nunaffected, because in those cases the genesis block is not marked as pruned.\n\nThe change does not start a reindex automatically, because recovering a pruned\nnode this way means downloading the whole chain again, which should be the user's\nchoice.\n\n## Testing\n\nfeature_reindex_init.py is extended to reproduce the state directly:\n\n1. Start a node with -fastprune -prune=1.\n2. Generate 400 blocks and prune, so genesis block data is removed.\n3. Stop the node and delete its chainstate directory.\n4. Assert startup fails with the new error instead of hanging.\n5. Allow the suggested reindex and assert the node comes back up at height 0.\n\nWithout the fix, step 4 never returns and the test hits the 60s startup timeout.\n\n## Verification\n\nBuilt and tested on macOS arm64 (Apple Clang 17):\n\n```sh\ncmake -B build -DENABLE_IPC=OFF\ncmake --build build -j10\nctest --test-dir build -j4\npython3 build/test/functional/test_runner.py -j10\n```\n\nAll runnable unit tests passed (script_assets_tests was skipped, its external\ntest data was not available). The default functional suite passed, as did the\nextended pruning/index tests (feature_pruning.py, feature_index_prune.py) and the\nassumeutxo tests. No new compiler warnings.\n\nNot tested: Linux/Windows CI, the Qt GUI path, the IPC build, and a real OOM\ninterruption (the test constructs the resulting on-disk state rather than\ntriggering an actual OOM).\n",
