      "message": "init: Fail if empty chainstate cannot be rebuilt\n\nA pruned node whose chainstate database is empty, and whose block index\nsays the genesis block has been pruned, never finishes starting up. An\nempty chainstate can only be rebuilt by connecting blocks from genesis,\nbut there is no block data left to connect. Init then waits forever for\na chain tip, without logging why.\n\nThis state is reached when the node is killed, for example by the OOM\nkiller, during the first flush of its chainstate if that flush also\nprunes block files: FlushStateToDisk() writes the block index, which\nmarks the pruned blocks as missing, before it writes the coins\ndatabase. Deleting the chainstate directory of a pruned node leads to\nthe same state. The report in #29422 shows an assertion failure in\ngetBlockHash() when an index is enabled. Current master hangs instead,\nwith or without an index.\n\nDetect this while loading the chainstate and return a FAILURE status.\nThe existing handling then tells the user to restart with -reindex, or\noffers to start the reindex in the GUI.\n\nFixes #29422.",
